Subject: [PATCH] ctrl: a policy ACK leaves a radio with its own request pending

0226 lets a Multi-AP Policy Config ACK configure every radio of the agent waiting in
set_policy_pending: em_config sends the agent's policy from one radio and the others wait for
it. It configured a radio with a request of its own outstanding as well (a set_policy command
on that radio, or a radio that sent in an earlier round): that radio's command completed and
its policy was committed to the model and the database though the agent had acknowledged
another request, and if that radio's request was lost the controller held a policy the agent
never applied.

Now the ACK configures the radio whose request it answers and the radios that sent none; a
radio with its own request outstanding stays in the step and sends again until its own ACK
arrives. A radio entering the step starts with no request outstanding, so the MID of a
cancelled request cannot hold it there.

Platform-independent (completes the lab's 0226); not for upstream on its own.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [completes 0226, a lab patch]

diff --git a/src/em/em.cpp b/src/em/em.cpp
index b38a778..c2c8e61 100644
--- a/src/em/em.cpp
+++ b/src/em/em.cpp
@@ -206,6 +206,8 @@ void em_t::orch_execute(em_cmd_t *pcmd)
             } else if ((pcmd->get_orch_op() == dm_orch_type_channel_pref) && (m_sm.get_state() == em_state_ctrl_ap_cap_report_received)) {
                 m_sm.set_state(em_state_ctrl_channel_query_pending);
             } else if ((pcmd->get_orch_op() == dm_orch_type_policy_cfg) && (m_sm.get_state() == em_state_ctrl_channel_queried)) {
+                // no request of its own yet: a cancelled one's MID must not hold it in the step
+                m_policy_req_msg_id = 0;
                 m_sm.set_state(em_state_ctrl_set_policy_pending);
             } else if ((pcmd->get_orch_op() == dm_orch_type_channel_sel) && (m_sm.get_state() == em_state_ctrl_configured)) {
                 m_sm.set_state(em_state_ctrl_channel_select_pending);
@@ -288,6 +290,7 @@ void em_t::orch_execute(em_cmd_t *pcmd)
             break;
 
 		case em_cmd_type_set_policy:
+            m_policy_req_msg_id = 0;
             m_sm.set_state(em_state_ctrl_set_policy_pending);
             break;
 
diff --git a/src/em/policy_cfg/em_policy_cfg.cpp b/src/em/policy_cfg/em_policy_cfg.cpp
index 23dbbed..60874b7 100644
--- a/src/em/policy_cfg/em_policy_cfg.cpp
+++ b/src/em/policy_cfg/em_policy_cfg.cpp
@@ -982,10 +982,13 @@ int em_policy_cfg_t::handle_1905_ack(unsigned char *buff, unsigned int len)
     }
     // The policy is the agent's: em_config sends it once, from the agent's
     // first radio, and the others wait in the same step. The ACK configures
-    // them too, or they stay in set_policy_pending.
+    // them too, or they stay in set_policy_pending. A radio with a request of
+    // its own outstanding waits for that request's ACK: another request's ACK
+    // does not acknowledge it, and it keeps sending until its own arrives.
     if (match_found) {
         for (auto &em : em_radios) {
-            if (em->get_state() == em_state_ctrl_set_policy_pending) {
+            if (em->get_state() == em_state_ctrl_set_policy_pending &&
+                    (em->m_policy_req_msg_id == 0 || em->m_policy_req_msg_id == response_msg_id)) {
                 em->m_policy_req_msg_id = 0;
                 em->set_state(em_state_ctrl_configured);
             }
